{
  "description": "Staged biology phase-cycle engine — the learner steps a Next/Prev cursor through an ordered roster of stages (e.g. mitosis phases), each revealing its own node/edge/shape snapshot, label, and description, and can predict the next stage before revealing it for immediate correct/incorrect feedback. Stage vocabulary is entirely config-declared, so the same mechanism serves any staged biology process, on a biology-canvas. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
